          <msContents>
            <summary>
              Excerpt of the Peace and Friendship Treaty concluded at Halifax on 10 March 1760 between Governor Charles Lawrence and Chief Paul Laurent of the LaHave Mi'kmaq, guaranteeing liberty of hunting and fishing, establishment of a Truckhouse at the River Chibenaccadie, and free liberty of trade at Halifax.
            </summary>
            <textLang mainLang="en">Eighteenth-century colonial legal English</textLang>
          </msContents>
